<!--Render Target Documentation — AssemblyPatterns
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.AssemblyPatterns-->
<rdoc:AssemblyPatterns xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Semantic MBOM values to SCAD assembly helper calls
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Assembly patterns exist in SCAD and have no BML equivalent. The renderer
    inserts them from the semantic MBOM value and the composition structure.
    The mapping table is declarative and configurable, not hardcoded in
    processor control flow.

    MBOM semantic value to SCAD output:

    - baseCutoutType = "groove" on a top part
      -> mb_assembly_groove(assembly, renderGroups, group_top)
    - tongue = true on a bottom part
      -> mb_assembly_tongue(assembly, renderGroups, group_bottom)
    - offset on an assembly-dependent part
      -> mb_assembly_offset([x, y, z], assembly, renderGroups, group_top)
    - render per part
      -> mb_group_render(renderGroups, group_bottom)
    - id per part
      -> mb_block_id(blockId, part_bottom)
    - baseAdjustment, namespace-filtered
      -> mb_params_filter(baseAdjustment, ns_bottom)

    For each composition child the renderer emits part variables inside the
    wrapper children block:

        part_bottom  = "bottom";
        group_bottom = part_bottom;
        ns_bottom    = part_bottom;

    The part name is the composition child id.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:LeafOptimization" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:AssemblyPatterns>
